### Login como ADMIN (guarda o token na variável "token"). Requer um usuário ADMIN já existente no banco
@admin_email = admin@example.com
@admin_password = change-me-123
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{admin_email}}",
  "password": "{{admin_password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Criar ANALYST -> 201
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "analyst@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ANALYST"
}

### Criar ADMIN -> 201
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "admin2@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### Criar com role CLIENT -> 400
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "CLIENT"
}

### Sem token -> 401
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "x@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ANALYST"
}



### Login (guarda o token na variável "token") -- com analista
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "analyst@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}
